AB  - The widespread adoption of large language models (LLMs) in software development has given rise to vibe coding—a practice in which developers rely on conversational prompts to generate and refine code. While this approach accelerates prototyping and lowers barriers to entry, it also introduces risks including frequent and unstable code changes, reduced readability, and a lack of accountability. To address these challenges, this paper proposes the Prompt–Refactor– Verify (PRV) cycle, a lean, human-centered framework that adapts prompt engineering techniques to AI-assisted programming.
